2. HOW KYC RENEWAL WORKS
   (OFFICIAL PATH)

    1. Sign in to the merchant
       dashboard by typing the
       address yourself
       (dashboard.paylane.example)
       -> Compliance -> KYC.
    2. Upload the listed
       documents:
       - Beneficial-owner ID
         (passport/national
         ID) where changed
         since the last cycle
       - Address proof if
         older than 3 months
       - Payout bank details:
         only changed when
         they actually change,
         and a payout-account
         change always triggers
         BOTH a dashboard
         confirmation AND a
         call to your
         registered number -
         never an SMS code
         collected through
         an emailed page.
    3. Review completes in
       5-7 days; payouts
       continue throughout.

  PayLane will NEVER:
  - Email a "KYC submission
    portal" collecting
    shareholder passports +
    payout account numbers +
    SMS verification codes
    in one session (that
    package is precisely
    what a payout-
    redirection attack
    needs; real re-
    verification of payout
    accounts happens inside
    the logged-in dashboard
    with a callback, not
    through emailed links)
  - Charge an "expedited
    review" fee (KYC review
    is a compliance
    obligation, free, and
    has no paid fast lane)
  - Threaten that two held
    cycles trigger
    "enhanced monitoring"
    to sell the expedited
    option (documents
    arriving by the stated
    deadline never hold
    payouts at all)
  - Use lookalike domains
    such as
    "paylane-compliance"
    or "pl-merchant"

3. VERIFY THIS NOTICE

  - KYC expiry and the
    document checklist are
    on the dashboard
    compliance page (typed
    address)
  - Your account manager
    confirms the cycle on
    the quarterly call
